WEBVTT

NOTE Visual narrative text; instrumental soundtrack with no speech.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Optimising Microsoft Teams. A research-led model for undergraduate learning. Kinon A. Southerton Jones.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.000
Teams was already part of university life.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
But the workflow still crossed platforms.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.600
63 questionnaire responses. 5 interviews. One six-member project.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.600
67% reported no formal Teams training. 36 of 54 answers.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.400
The tools existed. Using them well was the challenge.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.400
So I designed a more connected model.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.000
One Team, One Module. General for lecturers and all students; private group channels for project teams.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Module homepage: module information, learning resources, class schedule, assignments, recent files and lecturer information.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.400
Class Notebook: Content Library, Collaboration Space and individual student areas.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:48.600
Classwork: create an assignment, attach the brief, student view and assessment rubric.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:49.800
Student check-ins, too.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.000
Announcements stay with the module.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.800
Resources organised by topic.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.800
Each project group gets a private workspace.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.200
One shared report. One shared presentation.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.600
Tasks. Owners. Deadlines. Progress.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.400
Meetings leave a record.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.600
Ideas stay collaborative.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.400
Project risks stay visible.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.200
Quick conversations, close to the work.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:12.600
One connected academic workspace. A proposed model for undergraduate learning. Kinon A. Southerton Jones.
